- added stale-batch supersession handling, queued-cancel parity, and runner-survival on cancelled sync tools
- implemented the per-user-turn round cap with synthetic terminal tool-result frames
- fixed the final-tool race by marking the batch ready for followup before broadcasting the last result, and waiting for the originating generation task to finish before that followup can re-enter

In `bot.py` I removed the disabled conversation-cache env/config wiring from the `NemotronOmniAudioLLMService(...)` construction.

In tests I:
- replaced the old cache/internal-loop coverage with helper-only coverage
